@jplu Thank you for your reply! Here's my thoughts

1. In `run_tf_ner`, it doesn't make the "true" labels start from 1, so that's definitely a bug.

2. We can make `pad_token_label_id = -1`, as long as we also mask out all the non-first tokens inside each word (in function `convert_examples_to_features()`) so that there softmax output are not taken by the loss. I think this makes more sense because we only use the first token (wordpiece) of each word for the tagging, and don't care about the output of the other tokens. This method is also supported by some people like in here: https://www.vamvas.ch/bert-for-ner/

